Subject: [PATCH 3/3] build: --source <address> names where a modified build's source is
From: Office Kit
Date: 2026-10-18
Upstream: https://github.com/BRF-Tech/filex-office-editor (AGPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 2026 BRF Tech)
Base: v0.3.1 57dda3dae99af78eb26b3c64b69f1e3f711f0757 (the tag commit; the next main commit acc87f88da47 changes only README.md)
Apply: git -C <filex checkout> apply <this file>   (in order: 0001, 0002, 0003)
Modified: this patch changes filex-office-editor; see docs/office-editor-patches.md (Office Kit)

Office Kit: build-app.mjs --source: 수정판(패치 적용판)의 소스 위치를 법적 고지 줄에 넣는다. 안 주면 예전 그대로.

scripts/build-app.mjs takes --source <address> for a build made from
changed sources (a fork, a redistribution with patches of its own): the
notice under the editor names that address as where the source is,
instead of this project's tag (AGPL section 6), and the banner of each
built script says it is a modified build and where its source is.
Without it the bundle is byte for byte what it was.

